        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Woman’s petticoat of pink silk satin, lined with a undyed glazed worsted and wadded with a thin layer of wool.  It is quilted in running stitch with pink silk thread in a horizontal pattern of wide swags with bows and flowers around the hem and a diamond pattern of 1-½ inch (3.5 cm) squares, above.  The petticoat is made of 6 panels of silk, opening at the centre back with a pocket cut into the panel on the right side.\n\nThe petticoat was altered in the 19th century for fancy dress.  A pocket bag was sewn into the pocket opening and the waist tape and ties removed and replaced with a wide silk waistband with 2 hooks and eyes."@en ;
